WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:05.705
Ukraine's military says it destroyed
almost 70 aerial targets

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.342
launched by Russia
in its latest onslaught overnight.

00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:12.579
And that includes more than three dozen
cruise missiles,

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.982
as well as Iranian made drones
and a reconnaissance drone.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:20.387
A police official in Kiev says
residential buildings and infrastructure

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:24.691
in several districts were damaged,
but no one was killed or injured.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.862
This comes just a day after Ukraine said
Russia had launched one of its

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:32.832
largest
drone attacks to date against Kiev.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:36.669
CNN some analysis is in London
with the very latest for you.

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:41.041
Somehow Russia
ramping up missile and drone strikes

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:45.412
targeting the Ukrainian capital
just as crowds were marking Kiev day.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:50.483
Yes. So yet again overnight
there was a huge assault

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.886
by Russia on Ukraine, as you mentioned.

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:57.524
Some 67 air targets shot down,
according to Ukrainian officials.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:02.796
37 cruise missiles
and 29 drones were destroyed.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.899
Ukrainian officials
say that this latest assault was targeting

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:09.702
military facilities
and critical infrastructure.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:13.306
And it comes, as you mentioned,
just a day after on Sunday,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.778
Ukraine saw the largest assault
since the conflict began by drones.

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:24.217
Some 59 drones were shot
at Ukraine on Sunday.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.853
All but one were shot down.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.987
So there's a couple of things

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:31.891
to take away from from this news,
from this information, as you mentioned.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:37.130
It appears that Russia is ramping up
its attacks far from the front lines.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.801
Of course, this serves to terrorize
the citizens of Ukraine who are, again,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:46.172
not on that battlefield,
but it also expands Ukraine's

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.275
very valuable munitions
When you think about the drones

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.879
in particular, these are very low cost.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:58.284
They cost about 20 times less than
the missiles required to take them out.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:03.456
So it's a way of forcing Ukraine
to expend very valuable resources.

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:06.659
But for Ukrainian officials,
what they take away from

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:09.762
this is that their air
defense systems are working.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:12.632
Is that those weapons that help
that poured in

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.835
from Nieto and its allies,
those are effective.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.470
Those are saving lives.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.306
If you take, again, the example of the air
assault today.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.309
So far, no reports of casualties.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.913
That means they're able to be effective
in taking out.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.583
Again, these huge barrages
that are being fired by Russia.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.421
And so what more have you been able
to learn about these series of explosions

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:39.192
that have happened in and around
the Russian occupied cities of Mariupol?

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.296
So both Ukrainian backed officials
and Russian backed officials

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:46.633
giving indications
that the cities of Mariupol

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:51.905
and burned down were sites of exclusion
over the course of the last day.

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:55.141
What we understand and again, it's
great for you to pull up the map there

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.845
because these are two very important
cities, critical cities on the Sea

00:02:58.845 --> 00:02:59.379
of Azov.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.148
Mariupol in particular,
of course, has become emblematic

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:07.320
to Ukrainians of the brutality
of Russian forces after it was taken

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:11.224
in a monthslong siege last year
at the beginning of the conflict,

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:13.226
it is very much Russian occupied.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.329
So is Verdansk right now
Ukrainian backed officials there

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:21.768
saying that they were targeting sites
for the Russian military

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:26.673
in both those locations, at least
five sites were targeted in Verdun.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.142
Another site was targeted in Mariupol.

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:33.279
Russian officials did indicate that
their air defense systems were activated.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:34.714
What does all of this mean?

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:38.251
It means potentially
that we're looking at Ukrainian forces

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.620
conducting what they call
shaping operation.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:44.490
So taking up critical infrastructure,
critical Russian positions

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.959
ahead of this counteroffensive.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:49.729
Again, Alina, some of these reporting,
thank you for your continued coverage.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:00.573
So that

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.810
sound in there, you can see
as it lights up those images

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.513
of Ukrainian forces repelling an intense
barrage of Russian drone attacks.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:11.417
Ukraine's military says its forces
shot down nearly 70 drones

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.785
that were targeting Kiev.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.354
It's being called Russia's largest attack

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:18.291
to date on the capital city
using Iranian made drones notably.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:21.461
And it comes as CNN teams on the ground
heard several explosions in

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:22.428
Kiev overnight.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:26.165
Now, these Russian attacks also come
as Ukraine nears the launch of this

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:29.102
long awaited counteroffensive
we've been talking about.

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:33.706
One of Ukraine's top generals recently
posted this highly produced video.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.410
It shows Ukrainian troops
preparing for battle and ends with troops

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.848
chanting a message that calls for victory
for a decisive offensive.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.716
Joining us now with more, retired U.S.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.351
Army Major Mike Lyons.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.253
Good to see you. As always.

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.021
So when we

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:52.325
when we talk about this, what would this
potential counter offensive at this point?

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.260
What would it look like?
Yeah, just look at a map.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.796
You can see Russian forces
in two separate locations.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.231
I believe any counteroffensive

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:02.568
is going to cut these Russian forces
in half here and threaten Crimea.

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:05.138
I think that is the issue here
for the Ukrainian forces.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.306
But they're not going to do that

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.842
until they have the combined arms,
the shock effect, the tanks,

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:14.147
helicopters, Bradley fighting vehicles,
more men, more equipment.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.316
Russia still has had setbacks.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:20.753
Lost a lot of men, low morale,
but they're still Russia.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:24.290
They could go on the active defense and
they still are very formidable opponent.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:25.758
They certainly have time on their side.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:29.095
They can wait it out a bit longer in terms
of the counter-offensive and whether

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:32.799
whether plays a critical role
and when we start to see that offensive.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:36.202
Explain to us how weather plays
into all this Yes, weather and terrain.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:40.106
It's part of a commander's assessment
with regard to the tactical situation

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:40.740
on the ground.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.676
On a ground war, though not

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:47.747
like D-Day, for example, when weather
really impact the seas and the like.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.316
I think what you're going to see here,

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:53.152
the soil
where there's concern that, for example,

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:57.156
a satellite images show
that the soil is hardening up.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:57.924
It's a little better.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:06:00.860
That will provide, again, those tanks
a little more mobility on the ground.

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.363
The Ukraine military has the advantage.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.097
That's a home.

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:06.132
Then they know the terrain.
They know where the bridges are.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.068
They know where things are going.
But I think it's still a small effect.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.237
I think the combat forces
are really more important.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.706
I say. So give us a sense of of timing.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:15.174
I feel that we've been talking about this

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.343
for a long time,
this potential counteroffensive.

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:20.012
Are we approaching the right moment?

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.114
Yeah. We go back to you.

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.549
Go back to that
and you have to say that again.

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.786
They're not going to put their troops in
a situation where they're going to fail.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.454
They need to succeed.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.757
They do pick the time.
They pick the pace and location.

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:33.793
I'm not sure they have enough troops
ready to go.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.628
We haven't seen, for example, reports

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:38.498
of massing of equipment
in this in the areas in the south.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:41.901
We hear a lot of reports
about what's going on in this part

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.202
here in back mount in the west.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:46.272
But again, from from my perspective,
from a military perspective,

00:06:46.606 --> 00:06:48.841
I think this is where
the counter-offensive takes place.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.810
And we don't have that equipment
there yet.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.345
It's not ready to go.

00:06:52.345 --> 00:06:53.579
Any sense of when it might be?

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.349
Because, I mean, the spring offensive,
I think strategically

00:06:56.349 --> 00:07:00.086
is really important for Ukraine
to be able to show that they can do this.

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.721
Well, I think let's say

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:04.157
let's give it another 90 days
and assess the situation there.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.892
You still have these crews, for example,

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:09.061
some of the weapons systems, for example,
the tanks, the leopard, the Abrams.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.564
These are the things that are going
to make a difference.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.967
These are the shock effects
that will make a difference on the ground.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:18.004
And they're just not there training
troops and grief and fear.

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:20.072
We have troops in the United States still.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.741
The Patriot missiles have been effective.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:25.945
The way Ukraine wins is a combined arms
fight and synchronizing all these troops.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:26.612
That takes time.

